    "profile_text": {
        "body": "Thomson Reuters is a public company headquartered in Toronto, founded in 2008 and trading as TRI. Its website describes the company as delivering technology with purpose, empowering professionals to make faster decisions, gain sharper insights, and deliver greater impact. The company positions its AI as grounded in authoritative content, deep domain expertise, rigorous data governance, and expert support.\n\nThe company's AI products include CoCounsel, which it describes as built on principles of Fiduciary-Grade AI and as the AI of choice for professionals who need to deliver defensible work. CoCounsel Legal is an agentic AI for legal professionals, and the site reports that law firm Greenberg Traurig, LLP has deployed the next generation of CoCounsel Legal. The site also describes Westlaw AI and Practical Law content integration for research, analysis, and drafting, and says a customer, Justly Prudent, used CoCounsel and Westlaw AI to increase litigation capacity by 100%. Other AI tools mentioned include an AI-powered market intelligence tool for transactional attorneys, AI software for trade compliance and Harmonized System code classification, and ONESOURCE+ for tax, trade, legal, and risk.\n\nThe product record for CoCounsel (Casetext) describes it as a legal research AI product with litigation support and Westlaw integration, and notes attorney work product risk. There are no litigation cases or MCP servers associated with the company in the available data. The site also publishes reports, including the Future of Professionals Report 2026 and the 2026 AI in Professional Services Report, the latter drawing on perspectives from more than 1,500 professionals.",
